/* 2 · READOUT COACH — thesis-driven, play-reactive guidance for the arp-bar strip.
   Drop-in driver (handoff: ~/Desktop/signal-readout-handoff.md), replacing the MOCK cycler.
   Self-wiring: installs its own 600ms poll + passive listeners in readoutStart(), tears them
   down in readoutStop(). Edits NO other handler; reads engine getters + in-scope module state;
   writes ONLY #readout. 3-line model: a = action (bright, ▸), b = plain anchor (mid),
   c = next-step horizon (faint). Silent — text only — so it is fully verifiable headless.
   Compat stubs: the PARKED PLUCK seq code (readoutSeqOpen/Close, ~L2115/2129) still references
   the MOCK-era vars; kept inert here so those references stay safe no-ops. The `how`/"?" whisper
   from the handoff was dropped — there is no ? panel (#engdisc/#lpoverlay) in this build. */
let readoutTimer=null,readoutI=0,readoutCoachOn=false;const MOCK_TIPS=[];
const readoutEl=$('#readout');

